From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 04 Nov 2026 11:40:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Infer TileLang shared-memory alignment from every use

Upstream-base: tile-ai/tilelang@2123e412ce2217b324c50c4ec967213906456ac5
Local-base: b26f48b85790b832993f2c9d240dc3c39d6075e8, the five-patch refresh from deployment PR #875.
Upstream-source: https://github.com/tile-ai/tilelang/pull/3690
Upstream-head: 277f2cd48553fafc99802238f52b6f0146b49f12

Rationale: Infer shared-memory alignment from all buffer uses, including TMA descriptors, instead of conservatively aligning every arena to 1024 bytes.

Quality: Changes allocation alignment and padding, not arithmetic. Descriptor and swizzle constraints must remain satisfied. The recorded tests establish correctness and codegen behavior, not a serving speedup.

Tests: Nineteen alignment, packed-allocation and exact swizzled-TMA checks pass twice.
Recorded compiler tree: e9a38e6d7c7cb40db6f219b266288e03e6e3ad70.
See this candidate's results.json and immutable raw receipts. Full image,
retained-feature and serving qualification remain separate gates.

Upstream-status: open PR, checked 2026-11-04; pinned experimental backport.
Remove this local backport when advancing to an upstream revision containing it.
